    <comments>Fixture deck for scenario_combat_gate (.uitest/scenario.py), Player 1's side --
    live-verifies 2-player combat automation (doc/commander-status/phase8-combat.md's Stages
    A/B/C/D, GTest-only until now) together with the static/continuous-abilities anthem
    extension (doc/commander-status/phase8-static-abilities.md, also GTest-only until now):
    Glorious Anthem (&quot;Creatures you control get +1/+1.&quot;, {1}{W}) and Darksteel Myr
    (indestructible 1/1, {3}) -- attacking unblocked as a anthem-boosted 2/2 makes the anthem's
    combat-math effect directly observable as the defending player's exact life loss. Just these
    two cards, both drawn on turn 1: canDeclareAttacker() (rules_engine.cpp) only checks phase +
    active player, no summoning-sickness gate exists in this fork, so Myr can attack the same
    turn it's cast -- no need for a second turn (and thus no second Draw step to keep the
    library alive for). Both cards already in .uitest/sample_cards.xml.</comments>
